xcb: Harmattan multitouch from XInput 2.0 valuators

The N9's X server (1.9.5) speaks XInput 2.0, which has no touch events. Its touchscreen
driver (mtev) reports every finger in ordinary pointer events, as repeated groups of "Abs MT"
valuators (position, touch major and minor, pressure), each group ending with the finger's
tracking id. Qt 5.0-5.3 decoded them in qxcbconnection_maemo.cpp (behind
XCB_USE_XINPUT2_MAEMO, removed in 5.4; Copyright (C) 2013 Digia Plc); this is the same
decoding for the 5.15 plugin, through xcb-xinput, on servers older than XI 2.2 with a device
that has those valuators. The last finger lifted comes as a button release, which releases
every point. The pointer events count as synthesized from the touches, as with XI 2.2 pointer
emulation: Qt Quick takes the touch events, widgets keep their mouse events.

